msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:36
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:37
msgid ":ref:`cpn_potentiometer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:38
msgid ":ref:`cpn_i2c_lcd1602`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:42
msgid "2. Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:44
msgid "Open the ``10-Potentiometer_scale_value.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\fun_project\\10-Potentiometer_scale_value``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:52
msgid "3. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:54
msgid "The project functions by continually reading the value from a connected potentiometer. This value is then mapped to a smaller scale (0-16) and represented both numerically and visually on the LCD. By checking the difference between consecutive readings, the code ensures that only significant changes are reflected on the display, thereby reducing jitter. Reducing jitter helps avoid undesirable visual effects resulting from frequent refreshing of the LCD screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:56
msgid "**Library Inclusion and Initialization**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:64
msgid "Here, the required libraries (``Wire`` for I2C communication and ``LiquidCrystal_I2C`` for the LCD) are included. An LCD object is created with the I2C address ``0x27`` and is defined to have ``16`` columns and ``2`` rows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:66
msgid "**Variable Declaration**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:73
msgid "``lastRead`` stores the previously read potentiometer value. ``currentRead`` will store the current reading from the potentiometer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:75
msgid "**setup() Function**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:85
msgid "The LCD is initialized, its backlight is turned on, and serial communication is started at a baud rate of ``9600``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:87
msgid "**Main Loop**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:110
msgid "The potentiometer value is read and mapped to a bar length (0-16)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:111
msgid "If the difference between the last and current reading is more than ``2``, the LCD is updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:112
msgid "The value is printed on the first row and a bar (based on the mapped value) on the second row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:113
msgid "The value is also sent to the serial monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/10-fun-Potentiometer_scale_value.rst:114
msgid "Before the next iteration, ``lastRead`` is updated, and a delay of ``200ms`` is introduced for stability."
msgstr ""
